What changed:
- kubernetes: takes dist and version. Any other key gets a validate() line, and with distribution: <rke2|k3s> it says "write kubernetes: { dist: k3s }". kubernetes() refuses in the same words, and so do distribution, version and supervisor_port.
- kubernetes.version must be a string (empty or absent = the pin). validate() line, and version() refuses it.
- ssh: unknown key (not private_key or public_key): validate()-ONLY, my choice. Reason: in dev mode ocp destroy reads ssh: (ClusterKey _bootstrap_key -> ssh_private_key_path), and a refusal there skips the RKE2/K3s uninstall on the ssh machines. That is the k347/k323 rule. ssh_config refuses only the k340 shapes.
- A control plane's name: must be a string (@CP_NAME_KEYS, in the k340 host/address loop). cluster_status refuses it via _first_cp_string.
- An ssh pool's nodes: entry takes host (node_ip keeps its own line). validate()-only, kept out of _pool_nodes_errors (destroy, k323).
- ocp init --dist and the robocop Controller check against @OCP::Config::DISTRIBUTIONS. Messages unchanged.
- service: shape on a control plane: NOT touched, left for k357.
